# dev — web development reference lookups

## mdn — MDN Web Docs

  mdn <query>                 Search MDN, show top 5 results with summaries + URLs
  mdn <query> -o              Open top result in browser
  mdn <query> -n <count>      Show more results (default: 5)
  mdn <query> -n <count> -o   Show more results and open top in browser
  mdn -h, mdn --help         Show help
  mdn "fetch api"
  mdn "css grid" -o
  mdn "web workers" -n 10
  mdn "intersection observer" -n 3 -o

## cani — caniuse.com

  cani <feature>              Open caniuse.com search in browser (default)
  cani <feature> -u           Print URL only, do not open browser (pipeable)
  cani -h, cani --help       Show help
  cani "css grid"
  cani "webp"
  cani "container queries" -u

## goto — bookmarks

  goto                      List all bookmarks (sorted alphabetically)
  goto -g                   List all bookmarks with section groups
  goto <query>              Filter bookmarks by name/tag/description (sorted)
  goto -g <query>           Filter bookmarks, preserving section groups
  goto <query> -o           Open the matched URL in browser (first match)
  goto -u                   Print tag + URL only, do not open browser
  goto -c <category>        Filter by category (e.g., lang, 01-lang)
  goto -c <category> -g     Filter by category with groups preserved
  goto -a, goto --categories List all available categories
  goto -h, goto --help      Show help

  Categories (10 broad groups):
    01-lang     Programming Languages (Go, JS/TS, Node, Python, Rust, etc.)
    02-web      Web Development (MDN, caniuse, W3C, web.dev)
    03-data     Databases & Data (PostgreSQL, Redis, SQLite, etc.)
    04-infra    Infrastructure & DevOps (K8s, Docker, Podman, Terraform)
    05-cloud    Cloud Providers (AWS, GCP, Cloudflare)
    06-ai       AI & Machine Learning (HuggingFace, PyTorch, OpenAI, etc.)
    07-security  Security (OWASP, JWT, SSL Labs, CVE, etc.)
    08-net      Networking & Protocols (RFC, HTTP/2, HTTP/3, TLS, etc.)
    09-tools    General Development Tools (Git, Vim, tmux, regex, jq, etc.)
    10-work     Work & Local Development (local servers, projects, etc.)

  Bookmark files:
    topics/dev/bookmarks          Committed to dotfiles (shared)
    topics/dev/bookmarks.local    Gitignored (machine/work-specific)
    topics/dev/bookmarks.pending  Staging area for new bookmarks

  Format: <tag>  <url>  <description>
  Tip: use specific tags (goto go/docs) to guarantee a single match

## Notes
  MDN uses an undocumented but stable JSON search API — returns real summaries.
  caniuse has no per-feature CLI API — browser is the only real option.
  Browser opener: 'open' (macOS) or 'xdg-open' (Linux), detected automatically.
  Flags for mdn and goto can be combined in any order: mdn "css grid" -n 10 -o
  Bookmarks are organized into 10 Johnny Decimal-style categories (01-10) for easy filtering.
